course: dictionary
lesson: 15774
title: Tupi: a people, a language, and words we borrow
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one job, and a capital letter can be a clue. Tupi with a capital T is a name. It names a group of Indigenous peoples of Brazil, and it also names their family of languages. «The Tupi lived along the Atlantic coast when Europeans arrived.» Here Tupi is a people, not a thing you can eat or wear.
explain: Tupi can also work as an adjective, a word that tells you more about a noun. «She studied Tupi words for her school project.» Here Tupi describes the words, so it tells you which words she studied. Ask yourself: is this word a group, a thing, or a description? The sentence will show you.
explain: Some words travel between languages. Many English words came from Tupi through Portuguese, the language spoken in Brazil. «The toucan sat in the tree while the jaguar stayed hidden in the shade.» Two animal names in that sentence came from Tupi, so you have already met some of its words.
fact: Tupi is the name of a group of Indigenous peoples of Brazil.
fact: The Tupi lived along the Atlantic coast when Europeans arrived.
fact: Tupi is also the name of a family of languages.
fact: «Jaguar», «piranha», «toucan» and «tapioca» came into English from Tupi, through Portuguese.
fact: A capital letter, as in Tupi, often means a name of a people, a place or a language.
exercise: «The Tupi lived along the Atlantic coast when Europeans arrived.» In this sentence, what is Tupi? | *A group of people | A river in Brazil | A jungle animal | A kind of fruit
exercise: Which of these words came into English from Tupi, through Portuguese? | castle | bicycle | window | *jaguar
exercise: «She studied Tupi words for her school project.» In this sentence, Tupi is used as what? | A number | *An adjective, describing the words | A name of a school | A verb, an action
test: Tupi is also the name of what? | A kind of tree | A type of boat | A famous castle in Europe | *A family of languages
test: Piranha, toucan and tapioca all came into English from which source? | *Tupi, through Portuguese | Chinese, through trade | Latin, through French | Greek, through stories
exam: Why is Tupi written with a capital T in «She studied Tupi words for her school project»? | *It names a people and a language | It means very old | It is a made-up word | It is the first word of the sentence
